# Agent deployment and installation (MezzoRecovery)

Design work in this repo assumes the **MezzoRecovery central app** exposes a **download/bootstrap endpoint** so operators install the agent with a **single-line shell command** (e.g. `curl … | sudo bash -s -- --server … --token …`). Full narrative: `MezzoRecovery/prompts/agent-deployment.md`.

## Agent role

- **One privileged machine-level agent per machine**; it coordinates **all tape drives** on that host — not one service per drive.
- Primary target: **Linux** with **`systemd`**, **production-safe** and **automation-friendly**.

## Installation goals

- **Non-interactive by default**; copy/paste from UI; no “build from source” or manual tar+edit-service as the primary path.
- **Idempotent**: prefer **install-or-upgrade** — safe re-runs, preserve durable identity and intended config where appropriate; clear failures on conflict.
- **Explicit and auditable**: state what is downloaded, written, and executed; avoid opaque multi-stage remote execution.

## Packaging and runtime

- Ship **ready-to-run** artifacts (**self-contained**; **Native AOT** is in scope). **No .NET SDK** on the target.
- **Versioned** artifacts per RID (e.g. `linux-x64`, `linux-arm64`), e.g. `tar.gz` + optional checksum; central app exposes **stable bootstrap URL**, **metadata/latest**, and **versioned package** endpoints (exact routes are flexible).

## Bootstrap script responsibilities

- Strict shell (`set -euo pipefail` where applicable), validate **Linux / arch / systemd / root** and tools (`curl` or `wget`, `tar`).
- Download correct package, unpack, **write config** predictably, install **`systemd` unit**, **enable + start** (or restart), print **clear success/failure** and how to verify.

## Enrollment

- Prefer **short-lived enrollment token** from UI → written to config → exchanged on first run for **durable identity**; avoid long-lived secrets in install commands or world-readable token storage.

## Security

- **HTTPS only** for downloads; **no arbitrary remote shell** from server-supplied fragments; **integrity** (checksum/signed metadata) — call out gaps if not implemented yet.

## Lifecycle

- Design for future **uninstall / repair / reinstall** (stop/disable service, remove binaries, intentional preserve/remove of config and `/var/lib` identity).

## Avoid by default

- Docker/K8s as primary install, interactive wizards, multiple agents per machine, undocumented enrollment side effects, “generic remote execution” installers.
